.TH CBMAP_CREATE_MP 3 "2026-10-06" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cbmap_create_mp \- create a BST map with custom memory management procedures
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cbstmap.h>

cbmap cbmap_create_mp(ccol_data_type key_type,
                      ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *mmgmt_procs, char **err);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Creates a self-balancing BST map that allocates through the given memory
management procedures. The function is a thin inline wrapper over
cbmap_create_full(3). It gives NULL for the custom comparison procedure.
The map therefore uses the default order for key_type, as cbmap_create(3)
describes.

Every allocation that the map makes after the creation goes through these
procedures. This includes the allocations of an iterator over the map.
Destroy the map while these procedures are valid.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
key_type     Type of the keys that the map stores
mmgmt_procs  Memory management procedures, or NULL for the default
             allocator
err          Optional pointer that receives an error string on failure,
             or NULL
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A new map on success.
NULL on failure. When err is not NULL, *err is set to an error string.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The function reports a failure and does not stop the program. The
cbmap_construct_mp(3) and cbmap_init_mp(3) macros call ccol_fatal_err()
on a failure
Destroy the map with cbmap_destroy(3)
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cbmap_create (3),
.BR cbmap_create_full (3),
.BR cbmap_construct_mp (3),
.BR cbmap_init_mp (3),
.BR cbmap_destroy (3)
